{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Topics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/flatMap(_:)","doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/flatMapAndMergeError(_:)","doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/map(_:)","doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/mapAndMergeError(_:)","doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/mapFailureToSuccess(_:)","doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/mapFailureToSuccessAndErrorToFailure(_:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult","doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HMResult"}],"title":"Mapping Methods","roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Mapping-Methods","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"General-transformation","type":"heading","level":5,"text":"General transformation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Transforming a value, by applying a function to it using dot syntax, is sometimes an easier-to-read way to write code, and probably ought to be available on "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"every type","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func transform<Transformed, Error>(","  _ transform: (Self) throws(Error) -> Transformed",") throws(Error) -> Transformed {","  try transform(self)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"But that’s not specific to "},{"code":"Result","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and is not included in this package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"We "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"could","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" restrict the transformation to require mapping similar types of "},{"code":"Result","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, such as"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Result<Int, Never>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ➡️ "},{"code":"Result<String, any Error>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That would look like this:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func transform<NewSuccess, NewFailure, Error>(","  _ transform: (Self) throws(Error) -> Result<NewSuccess, NewFailure>",") throws(Error) -> Result<NewSuccess, NewFailure> {","  try transform(self)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Even with this new restriction, the possibilities are so vast in what can be accomplished there, that it’s not worth creating a function for. And so again, this "},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not included in this package either."}]},{"anchor":"flatMap","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"flatMap"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the closest to a general-purpose "},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method that this package works with. The capabilities are different in only two respects:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure operates only on a wrapped value, instead of an entire ","type":"text"},{"code":"Result","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot modify the wrapped error type.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The “"},{"code":"flat","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"” in "},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" refers to the way that it introduces no more “nesting” than the "},{"code":"Result","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" represented before transformation. For example,"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Result<String, Never>.flatMap"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":", when supplied with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure returning type","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Result<Int, Never>"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":", will return","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Result<Int, Never>"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":", as opposed to an “unflattened”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Result<Result<Int, Never>, Never>"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"As documented below","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/flatMap(_:)","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"As documented below","type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"type":"text","text":" will not throw an error when the transformed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"failure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but it will throw an error if the transformation throws an error."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swift\/result\/flatMap(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" nearly gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" right, but it does not incorporate throwing an error. This version should be deprecated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"flatMapAndMergeError","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"flatMapAndMergeError"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a special case of ","type":"text"},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws the untransformed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" type, the error can be forwarded into the transformed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"type":"text","text":" type, rather than being thrown from "},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both forms are useful. Naming this differently than "},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is necessary because it would not be enough, for the compiler, to just add ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"text":" in front of another ","type":"text"},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overload.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"map","type":"heading","text":"map"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The only difference between "},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" is that map’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure returns a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Success"},{"text":", not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"type":"text","text":". Thusly, no “flattening” is necessary."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As with "},{"code":"flatMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swift\/result\/map(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" nearly gets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" right, but it does not incorporate throwing an error. This version should be deprecated."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"mapAndMergeError","text":"mapAndMergeError"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"flatMapAndMergeError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"flatMapFailure","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"flatMapFailure"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the same idea as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"type":"text","text":", except, with a transformation of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" type, rather than its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Success"},{"type":"text","text":" type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As we’ve seen above with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":", the standard library nearly gets this right, under the problematic* name "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swift\/result\/flatMapError(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but it does not incorporate throwing an error. It "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"should"}]},{"type":"text","text":", for completeness, but does anyone need that? 🤔 (It won’t be included in this package until we hear that they do.)"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"* It’s problematic because the failure type, while restricted to be an error, is called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":". And it’s not clear whether you’re mapping a failure enumeration case, or an error occurring from the transformation closure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"mapFailure","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"mapFailure"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMapFailure"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" is to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"mapFailureToSuccess","text":"mapFailureToSuccess"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This idea only works when the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" type is going to be “removed”, which is represented by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Never"},{"type":"text","text":". So, there’s no point in offering a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMapFailureToSuccess"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result.failure"},{"type":"text","text":"s can’t be created with if their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Never"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"mapFailureToSuccessAndErrorToFailure","type":"heading","text":"mapFailureToSuccessAndErrorToFailure"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a niche type of error mapping operation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s similar to the two “"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…AndMergeError"},{"type":"text","text":"” methods in that an error thrown from transforming will become a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"failure"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"But it’s dissimilar in that while the error thrown "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"can"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":", there’s no requirement of that (and it’s likely to be a rare case). So, calling this "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mapFailureToSuccessAndMergeError"},{"type":"text","text":" would not generally be accurate."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hmresult\/mapping-methods"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://HMResult/documentation/HMResult/Swift/Result/mapFailureToSuccess(_:)":{"type":"topic","title":"mapFailureToSuccess(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/hmresult\/swift\/result\/mapfailuretosuccess(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Transform failures into successes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HMResult\/documentation\/HMResult\/Swift\/Result\/mapFailureToSuccess(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mapFailureToSuccess"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":">(("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Failure"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Success"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6ResultO"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Success"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Never","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://HMResult/documentation/HMResult/Swift/Result/map(_:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/docume